			Microcomputer Blocks-World

MicroSHRDLU is a program for "robotically" manipulating an on-screen 3-D color
micro-world consisting of a tabletop and some blocks.  It is capable of 
natural-language spatial-vocabulary "understanding"; the user communicates 
English commands and queries via keyboard.  The software has "mind-reading" 
capacity for display of its internal parsing and planning processes.  
Provides a hands-on environment for exploring prospects and limits for AI.

Equipment:  MicroSHRDLU requires full IBM compatibility with either EGA or VGA
color graphics card and monitor.


MicroSHRDLU requires no special installation procedures, and is invoked by
typing the command MS at the DOS prompt.


For further information, see HELP in the program.

